module cli
    layer: DOMAIN
    version: 0.1.0
    intent: "FIXME(adopt): say in one sentence what this module is responsible for, and what it leaves to other modules. The Python file's docstring began: 'The command line: one sub-command per job done at the counter.' — use that if it is true, rewrite it if it is not. Also choose this module's layer: the draft wrote DOMAIN because nothing in the file said which layer this is, and the four layers are DOMAIN, APPLICATION, INFRASTRUCTURE or PRESENTATION. A module sits at exactly one layer and every declaration in it shares that layer. The rule that settles it: a module may only use modules at its own layer or below — DOMAIN may use DOMAIN and FRAMEWORK only, APPLICATION may also use DOMAIN, and PRESENTATION and INFRASTRUCTURE may use DOMAIN and APPLICATION — so the answer is the layer that lets this module import what it already imports."
    exports: [build_parser, main]

    requires:
      - argparse
      - bookshelf.config:DATA_DIR
      - bookshelf.config:LIBRARY_NAME
      - bookshelf.errors:BookshelfError
      - bookshelf:api
